Package: querra-fence-panel
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: Cosmin B. Memetea <CosminBMemetea@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: curl, bash, python3
Recommends: chromium-browser | chromium | firefox, libnotify-bin, zenity
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Homepage: https://cosminbmemetea.github.io/querra-fence/
Description: Querra Fence (safe fence) panel launcher for the Jetson desktop
 Adds a "Querra Fence" app to the GNOME dock. One click starts the QUERRA
 Fence panel if it is not running and opens it in an app window. Right-click
 actions start the ROS 2 demo, show the Foxglove address and restart the
 panel. Installing a newer version replaces the old one and keeps the dock
 icon where the user left it. The panel itself is not installed or changed;
 field-mode autostart is left as it is.
